  <section class="static-page__callout">
    <h2>Calculators and education—not personal advice</h2>
    <p>Finova provides financial calculators and general educational information. Merely using the website does not create financial, investment, tax, legal, accounting, lending or fiduciary advice.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Calculator results</h2>
    <p>Unless a page explicitly states otherwise, results are estimates based on the information entered and the methodology shown. Incorrect, incomplete or unsuitable inputs will produce an unsuitable result.</p>
    <p>Actual financial products may use different rates, fees, payment dates, compounding conventions, rounding, eligibility conditions or contractual terms.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Loans and salary</h2>
    <p>Loan schedules can differ from lender statements because of daily-interest conventions, floating-rate changes, fees, insurance and payment timing. Salary and in-hand estimates vary with employer structures, payroll rules and deductions.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Investment projections</h2>
    <p>SIP, compound-interest, FD, PPF and EPF results are projections based on the rates and contribution assumptions entered. They are not promises or guarantees of future returns. Market-linked values may rise or fall.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tax and statutory calculations</h2>
    <p>Tax calculations depend on the selected assessment year, income types, regime, deductions and user inputs. The focused income-tax calculator does not cover every exemption, special-rate income, surcharge or individual circumstance.</p>
    <p>EPF, PPF and gratuity rules, rates and entitlements can change. A calculator cannot determine legal eligibility for every employment or statutory situation.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Important decisions</h2>
    <p>Verify material decisions using applicable product documents, employer records, lender statements, government portals and qualified professionals. Finova does not recommend a specific financial product, provider, tax regime or course of action.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>No professional relationship</h2>
    <p>Using the website does not create an adviser-client, accountant-client, lawyer-client, lender-borrower or fiduciary relationship.</p>
  </section>
